theory.intro:
A line graph plots points and joins them, usually to show how something changes over time. You read values by following the scales on the two axes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,5.6); \draw[->] (0,0)--(8.0,0);
\foreach \y/\lab in {1/5,2/10,3/15,4/20} {\draw (-0.15,\y)--(0,\y); \node[left,font=\small] at (-0.15,\y) {$\lab$};}
\node[left,font=\small] at (-0.15,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x/\lab in {1/9am,2.6/10am,4.2/11am,5.8/12pm} {\draw (\x,0)--(\x,-0.15); \node[below,font=\small] at (\x,-0.15) {\lab};}
\draw[thick] (1,1)--(2.6,3)--(4.2,3)--(5.8,1.4);
\foreach \p in {(1,1),(2.6,3),(4.2,3),(5.8,1.4)} {\fill \p circle (2.5pt);}
\draw[dashed] (5.8,0)--(5.8,1.4)--(0,1.4);
\node[font=\small] at (1.4,2.6) {rises};
\node[font=\small,above] at (3.4,3.05) {level};
\node[font=\small] at (6.2,2.5) {falls};
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.5,2.5) {Water level (cm)};
\node[below] at (3.4,-1.0) {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.question_text:
The graph shows the water level in a tank.
(a) What was the water level at 10 am?
(b) During which interval did the level stay unchanged?
(c) Describe the changes from 9 am to 1 pm.
(d) How much did the level decrease from noon to 1 pm?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=14mm,y=2mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,xstep=14mm,ystep=10mm] (0,0) grid (4,30);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,32);
\foreach \y in {0,5,10,15,20,25,30} {\draw[black] (-0.08,\y)--(0,\y);\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\lab in {0/9 am,1/10 am,2/11 am,3/12 noon,4/1 pm} {\draw[black] (\x,0)--(\x,-0.8);\path (\x,-1) node[below,rotate=45,anchor=east,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {\lab};}
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,10)--(1,20)--(2,20)--(3,25)--(4,15);
\foreach \p in {(0,10),(1,20),(2,20),(3,25),(4,15)} {\fill[graphblue] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\path (-0.85,15) node[rotate=90] {Water level (cm)};
\path (2,-10) node {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

