workedExamples.solution_text:
10:30 am is halfway between 10 am and 11 am. Read up to the line, then across to the temperature axis.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=14mm,y=2mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{graphblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{guideorange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}
\definecolor{gridgrey}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\draw[gridgrey,xstep=14mm,ystep=10mm] (0,0) grid (4,30);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(4.3,0);
\draw[black,->] (0,0)--(0,32);
\foreach \y in {0,5,10,15,20,25,30} {\path (0,\y) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\y$};}
\foreach \x/\lab in {0/9 am,1/10 am,2/11 am,3/12 noon,4/1 pm} {\path (\x,-1) node[below,rotate=45,anchor=east,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {\lab};}
\draw[graphblue,thick] (0,10)--(1,15)--(2,25)--(3,25)--(4,20);
\foreach \p in {(0,10),(1,15),(2,25),(3,25),(4,20)} {\fill[graphblue] \p circle (1.5pt);}
\draw[guideorange,dashed,thick] (1.5,0)--(1.5,20)--(0,20);
\fill[guideorange] (1.5,20) circle (2pt);
\path (1.5,20) node[above left] {10:30 am};
\path (-0.85,15) node[rotate=90] {Temperature ($^{\circ}$C)};
\path (2,-10) node {Time};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The estimated temperature is $20^{\circ}\text{C}$.

